  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shailesh Kumar Srivastava vs State Of U.P. on 4 May, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?In Chamber Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 12473 of 2020 Applicant :- Shailesh Kumar Srivastava Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Krishna Murari Tripathi Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272 I.P.C is unjustified. Offence under sections 60/63 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 28.01.2020, who is not a previous convict.",
    "arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail. Shailesh Kumar Srivastava vs State Of U.P. on 4 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/141087422/ 1 Let the applicant, Shailesh Kumar Srivastava, involved in Case Crime No.0028 of 2020, under Sections 419, 420, 467, 468, 471, 272 I.P.C and 60/63 of Excise Act, Police Station Mugal Sarai, District- Chandauli be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned subject to following conditions.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail. Shailesh Kumar Srivastava vs State Of U.P. on 4 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/141087422/ 1 Let the applicant, Shailesh Kumar Srivastava, involved in Case Crime No.0028 of 2020, under Sections 419, 420, 467, 468, 471, 272 I.P.C and 60/63 of Excise Act, Police Station Mugal Sarai, District- Chandauli be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned subject to following conditions."
  },
